About Capco
Capco is a global technology and management consultancy dedicated to the financial services industry. We combine innovative thinking with unrivalled industry knowledge, to offer our clients consulting expertise, complex technology and package integration, transformation delivery and managed services to move their organizations forward.
• We specialize primarily in banking &amp; payments, capital markets, wealth &amp; asset management, insurance and energy
• We have a collaborative and efficient approach
• We help our clients successfully innovate, increase revenue, manage risk and regulatory change, reduce costs and enhance controls
• We serve our clients from 32 offices across the Americas, Europe, and Asia Pacific
If creativity and innovation are your passion, then Capco is right for you. You can grow in an inclusive, diverse and collaborative environment. At Capco, we will train and support you to help accelerate your career. &nbsp;
&nbsp;
The Role
As a Finance Data Engineer at Capco, you will work at the intersection of IT, Data and Finance, supporting the evolution of a critical Finance Data Mart used for Business Finance information, MI and reporting in Private Banking as well as other Banking areas. &nbsp;
The platform is a key source of financial information, supporting measures including such as Assets under Management (AuM), Net New Money (NNM) and Return on Assets (RoA) and other KPIs.&nbsp; &nbsp;
You will combine technical and data expertise with Finance understanding, enabling you to interpret and validate financial outputs, identify issues and help improve the quality and capabilities of the platform. &nbsp;
&nbsp;
&nbsp;
YOUR CAPCO DAY &nbsp;
• Work on the enhancement, upgrade, and potential re-development of a critical Finance Data Mart and its underlying data capabilities. &nbsp;
• Analyse and work with Business Finance data used to produce MI and reporting, including measures such as AuM, NNM and RoA and other critical KPIs in Private Banking. &nbsp;
• Use your Finance understanding to test and validate data outputs, identify inconsistencies, and ensure that information produced by the platform makes sense from a Business Finance perspective. &nbsp;
• Work closely with IT, Data and Finance stakeholders to translate Finance requirements into robust data and technical solutions. &nbsp;
• Contribute as part of a global team to improve the quality, reliability and future capabilities of a critical source of Business Finance information. &nbsp;
&nbsp;
&nbsp;
&nbsp;
YOUR CAPCO-FIT &nbsp;
&nbsp;
&nbsp;
• Deep experience in Data and IT, with strong database knowledge and hands-on SQL skills, alongside an understanding of coding and data engineering concepts. &nbsp;
• A strong understanding of Finance that enables you to interpret financial information, understand Business Finance reporting, and critically assess the outputs produced from underlying data. &nbsp;
• The ability to bridge Data, IT and Finance, translating between technical implementation and the financial meaning and purpose of the information being produced. &nbsp;
• Strong analytical skills with the ability to test and validate outputs, investigate discrepancies, identify errors and recommend improvements. &nbsp;
• Professional proficiency in English, as you will work within a global team where English is the working language. &nbsp;
&nbsp;
BONUS POINTS FOR&nbsp;
• Professional proficiency in French. &nbsp;
• Experience with Finance Data Marts, management information or Business Finance reporting within banking or financial services. &nbsp;
• Knowledge of private banking metrics and measures such as Assets under Management (AuM), Net New Money (NNM) and Return on Assets (RoA). &nbsp;
• Experience working with data environments supporting core banking platforms. &nbsp;
• Experience contributing to the enhancement, migration or re-development of complex data platforms. &nbsp;
&nbsp;
WHY CAPCO
A career at Capco is a chance to help reshape the competitive landscape in financial services. We launch new banks, transform existing ones, and help our clients navigate complex change. As consultants, we work on the front-end business design all the way through to technology implementation.
We are the largest Financial Services focused consultancy in the world, serving everyone from global banks to emerging FinTechs, from strategy through digital transformation, design, business consulting, data and analytics, cyber, cloud, technology architecture, and engineering.
Capco is a young and growing firm. We maintain an entrepreneurial spirit and growth mindset, and have minimal bureaucracy. We have no internal silos that get in the way of your career opportunities or ability to focus on our clients and make a difference to the business. We offer the opportunity for everyone to learn rapidly, take on tough challenges, and get promoted quickly. We take pride in our creative, collaborative, diverse, and inclusive culture, where everyone can #BYAW.
We offer highly competitive benefits, flexible working hours, technical and soft skills training, smartphone &amp; fast mobile internet and a work culture focused on innovation and creation of lasting value for our clients and employees.
&nbsp;
Ready to take the Next Step&nbsp;
If this sounds like you, we would love to hear from you. &nbsp;This is an opportunity to make a difference and contribute to a highly successful company with a significant growth trajectory.
